Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 05:16:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Add zmij license notice to COPYING

The shortest-digit float printer and its SSE2 digit routine are
adapted from zmij, which is MIT licensed. Also mention the copyright
in the source comments.
---
 COPYING                        | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/code/zmij.lisp             |  3 ++-
 src/compiler/x86-64/array.lisp |  8 ++++----
 3 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/COPYING b/COPYING
index 4220b3397..711ea7e57 100644
--- a/COPYING
+++ b/COPYING
@@ -17,9 +17,14 @@ the FreeBSD licence where not.
 
 The CityHash mix function as adapted in hopscotch.c has an MIT license.
 
+The zmij float printing code in src/code/zmij.lisp (and the SSE2 digit
+conversion in src/compiler/x86-64/array.lisp) is adapted from zmij
+(https://github.com/vitaut/zmij), which has an MIT license; its notice
+is included below.
+
 Thus, there are no known obstacles to copying, using, and modifying
-SBCL freely, as long as copyright notices of MIT, Symbolics, Xerox and
-Gerd Moellmann are retained.
+SBCL freely, as long as copyright notices of MIT, Symbolics, Xerox,
+Gerd Moellmann and Victor Zverovich are retained.
 
 ================================================================================
 
@@ -121,3 +126,31 @@ Gerd Moellmann are retained.
 ;;; software is freely granted, provided that this notice
 ;;; is preserved.
 ;;; ====================================================
